# Line endings for GENERATED artefacts.
#
# Several tests assert that a committed file is byte-for-byte what its generator
# produces today -- test_ccm_matrix, test_call_surface, test_iam_surface, and the
# `--check` mode of every scripts/*benchmark.py. The generators all write LF
# (`newline="\n"`), and git stores these blobs as LF. But this repository is worked
# on with `core.autocrlf=true`, which materialises them as CRLF on checkout, so the
# comparison fails on a fresh Windows clone with nothing actually wrong. It failed
# exactly that way when the CCM branch was merged.
#
# Pinning eol=lf changes only how the working tree is written -- the blobs are
# already LF, so this produces no index churn -- and it makes "regenerate and see no
# diff" true on every platform. Without it the alternative is to teach each test to
# ignore line endings, which is the same fix applied N times and forgotten on N+1.

# Generated data and documents.
compliance/ccm/*.yaml   text eol=lf
compliance/*.json       text eol=lf
docs/*.md               text eol=lf
tests/*_baseline.py     text eol=lf

# The deploy artefacts are compared against each other by test_terraform_parity.
deploy/**/*.yaml        text eol=lf
deploy/**/*.tf          text eol=lf
